   "text": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# release-notes\n\n## What it does\n\nDrafts release notes from merged PRs between two tags. `release-notes` gathers the PRs and drafts the notes; `technical-writing` edits prose.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse it when you want a release-notes draft for a tag range. It runs only when invoked manually:\n\n```text\n/release-notes <from-tag> <to-tag>\n```\n\nBoth tags must exist, and `gh` must be signed in. The skill stops before drafting if either tag is missing or `gh auth status` fails.\n\n## How it works\n\nIt groups PRs by Conventional Commit type, with features, fixes, and breaking changes first. PRs labeled `skip-notes` are excluded.\n\nEach breaking change needs a migration line. If the PR body has none, the draft marks it `TODO: migration`.\n\n## What you get\n\nA `RELEASE_NOTES.md` file in the working tree. The skill writes the draft and stops. It never publishes.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) Will it publish a release?\n(b) How do you run it?\n(c) What happens to a breaking change with no migration note?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (a) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
